 35S  c  1984Ca14: 30-1500-keV neutrons were produced from the Oak Ridge        
 35S 2c  Electron Linear Accelerator (ORELA). The target was 94.33%-enriched    
 35S 3c  {+34}S with a 5.54% impurity of {+32}S. Neutrons were detected using a 
 35S 4c  2-cm-thick and 7.5-cm in diameter NE110 proton-recoil detector. Prompt 
 35S 5c  |g rays from neutron capture were detected using two nonhydrogenous    
 35S 6c  fluorocarbon scintillators (NE-226). Measured |s(E{-n}). Deduced 81    
 35S 7c  resonances, J, |p, L, widths and spectroscopic factors by comparing the
 35S 8c  R-matrix predictions of the cross section with the data.               
 35S  c  2018MuZY: Atlas of Neutron Resonances. Evaluation of neutron resonance 
 35S 2c  energies, spins, width parameters, and resonance strengths for nuclei  
 35S 3c  of Z=1-60.                                                             
 35S  cL $J|p and L are from 2018MuZY. Resonance parameters E{-n}, g|G{-n},     
 35S 2cL |G{-|g}, and g|G{-n}|G{-|g}/|G are from 1984Ca14 due to significant    
 35S 3cL discrepancies, including orders of magnitude inconsistencies, between  
 35S 4cL the 1984Ca14 original data and 2018MuZY evaluation.                    
 35S 5cL g|G{-n}=(2J+1)|G{-n}/2.                                                
